\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  \textbf  {Protein mass data of distinct protein sectors under diverse growth conditions taken from Schmidt et al. \cite  {schmidtQuantitativeConditiondependentEscherichia2016}}: (A) All proteins represented by the iML1515 GEM and found in the proteomic data set, comprising the active and unused enzymes sectors. (B) Translational sector covering proteins assigned to the COG (Clusters of Orthologous Groups) class "translation, ribosomal structure, and biogenesis," which are not included in the iML1515. The black lines in panels A and B are linear fits of the data points resulting in the shown equations and coefficients of determination R2 . (C) Sum of the protein mass concentrations shown in panels A and B. The horizontal black line marks the 81\% of measured protein mass used to constrain protein availability in the PAM. Glucose chemostat and batch experiments are highlighted in blue and red, respectively. Note that protein concentrations relative to the cell dry weight (cdw) were related to the total protein concentration of 0.32 $g\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}g^{-1}_{cdw}$ measured by Schmidt et al \cite  {schmidtQuantitativeConditiondependentEscherichia2016}. \textbf  {Both figure and caption taken from \cite  {alterProteomeRegulationPatterns2021}}. }}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:proteome-allocation-patterns}{{1}{2}{\textbf {Protein mass data of distinct protein sectors under diverse growth conditions taken from Schmidt et al. \cite {schmidtQuantitativeConditiondependentEscherichia2016}}: (A) All proteins represented by the iML1515 GEM and found in the proteomic data set, comprising the active and unused enzymes sectors. (B) Translational sector covering proteins assigned to the COG (Clusters of Orthologous Groups) class "translation, ribosomal structure, and biogenesis," which are not included in the iML1515. The black lines in panels A and B are linear fits of the data points resulting in the shown equations and coefficients of determination R2 . (C) Sum of the protein mass concentrations shown in panels A and B. The horizontal black line marks the 81\% of measured protein mass used to constrain protein availability in the PAM. Glucose chemostat and batch experiments are highlighted in blue and red, respectively. Note that protein concentrations relative to the cell dry weight (cdw) were related to the total protein concentration of 0.32 $g\,g^{-1}_{cdw}$ measured by Schmidt et al \cite {schmidtQuantitativeConditiondependentEscherichia2016}. \textbf {Both figure and caption taken from \cite {alterProteomeRegulationPatterns2021}}}{figure.1}{}}
